<div class="arcade" data-unit-arcade>
 <div class="arcade-head"><p class="eyebrow">PATTERN MACHINE MISSION</p><h3>Restore five control modules</h3><p>Every repair uses a different Unit 1 representation. Accuracy unlocks the final recommendation; there is no timer.</p><div class="power" role="progressbar" aria-label="Modules restored" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="5" aria-valuenow="0" data-power-track><span data-power style="width:0%"></span></div><strong data-power-label>0 / 5 modules restored</strong></div>
 <div class="missions">
  <fieldset data-mission data-answer="2" data-success="The digit sum is 9, so 1,134 is divisible by 9; 9 is the largest offered group size." data-repair="The number passes 3, 6, and 9. The gate asks for the largest valid group."><legend><span>1</span><b>Shipment Gate</b> Which line can package 1,134 items using the largest valid group?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-1" value="0"/> groups of 3</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-1" value="1"/> groups of 6</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-1" value="2"/> groups of 9</label><button type="button" data-test>Test gate</button><p data-feedback role="status">Use divisibility evidence.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-mission data-answer="1" data-success="The display grows by 4 each time, and 4n+1 gives 5 when n=1." data-repair="The constant change becomes the coefficient. Then test the rule at figure 1."><legend><span>2</span><b>Light Pattern Generator</b> A display has 5, 9, 13, 17 lights. Which rule predicts figure n?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-2" value="0"/> 5n+4</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-2" value="1"/> 4n+1</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-2" value="2"/> n+4</label><button type="button" data-test>Test generator</button><p data-feedback role="status">Separate growth from the fixed part.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-mission data-answer="0" data-success="Substituting x=6 gives y=3(6)+2=20." data-repair="Keep x as the input and calculate the matching output using multiply, then add."><legend><span>3</span><b>Table Control Panel</b> The rule is y=3x+2. Which row repairs the table?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-3" value="0"/> x=6, y=20</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-3" value="1"/> x=6, y=18</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-3" value="2"/> x=20, y=6</label><button type="button" data-test>Test panel</button><p data-feedback role="status">Substitute the input.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-mission data-answer="2" data-success="When x=2, y=3(2)+2=8, so the point is (2,8)." data-repair="Evaluate y for the first coordinate, then keep the ordered pair in (x,y) order."><legend><span>4</span><b>Graph Console</b> Which point belongs to the same y=3x+2 relation?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-4" value="0"/> (8,2)</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-4" value="1"/> (2,6)</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-4" value="2"/> (2,8)</label><button type="button" data-test>Test console</button><p data-feedback role="status">Coordinates are input, then output.</p></fieldset>
  <fieldset data-mission data-answer="1" data-success="Division undoes multiplication. Dividing both sides by 4 preserves equality and gives x=9." data-repair="Choose the inverse of multiplying by 4 and apply it to both sides, not only one side."><legend><span>5</span><b>Packing Balance</b> A record says 4x=36. Which repair preserves equality and finds x?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-5" value="0"/> subtract 4 from one side</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-5" value="1"/> divide both sides by 4</label><label><input type="radio" name="arcade-5" value="2"/> add 36 to both sides</label><button type="button" data-test>Test balance</button><p data-feedback role="status">Use the inverse operation on both sides.</p></fieldset>
 </div>
 <div class="control-room" data-control-room hidden tabindex="-1"><p class="eyebrow">FINAL CONTROL ROOM</p><h3>Recommend a reliable way to check the repaired machine.</h3><label>Use at least three Unit 1 representations.<textarea rows="5" data-final placeholder="First I would… This connects to… I would verify by…"></textarea></label><button type="button" data-final-check>Send recommendation</button><p data-final-feedback role="status">Your explanation should connect, not merely list, representations.</p></div>
</div>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-unit-arcade]').forEach(root=>{const missions=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-mission]')];let unlocked=false;const update=()=>{const complete=missions.filter(x=>x.dataset.complete==='true').length;const power=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-power]');if(power)power.style.width=`${complete/5*100}%`;const track=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-power-track]');track?.setAttribute('aria-valuenow',String(complete));const label=root.querySelector('[data-power-label]');if(label)label.textContent=`${complete} / 5 modules restored`;const room=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-control-room]');if(room){room.hidden=complete<5;if(complete===5&&!unlocked){unlocked=true;room.focus()}}};missions.forEach(item=>item.querySelector('[data-test]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const chosen=item.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked');const feedback=item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-feedback]');if(!chosen){if(feedback)feedback.textContent='Choose a repair before testing.';item.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input')?.focus();return}const ok=chosen.value===item.dataset.answer;item.dataset.complete=String(ok);item.classList.toggle('restored',ok);if(feedback)feedback.innerHTML=`<strong>${ok?'Module restored.':'Signal mismatch.'}</strong> ${ok?item.dataset.success:item.dataset.repair}`;update()}));root.querySelector('[data-final-check]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const text=(root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('[data-final]')?.value||'').toLowerCase();const terms=['rule','table','graph','point','equation','tile','divis','expression'].filter(x=>text.includes(x));const f=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-final-feedback]');if(f)f.innerHTML=terms.length>=3&&text.length>=100?'<strong>Mission complete.</strong> Your recommendation connects at least three representations and provides a verification path.':'<strong>Strengthen the recommendation.</strong> Connect at least three of: divisibility rule, expression, pattern, table, graph, equation, or tile model—and explain how one verifies another.'});update()});
</script>
<style>
.arcade{border-radius:17px;overflow:hidden;background:#17152e;color:#fff}.arcade-head{padding:1.2rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at top right,#3f3c85,#17152e 60%)}.arcade-head h3{font-size:1.7rem;margin:.2rem 0}.power{height:12px;margin-top:1rem;border-radius:99px;background:#ffffff1c;overflow:hidden}.power span{display:block;height:100%;background:#76e0b7;transition:width .25s}.missions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:.8rem;padding:1rem}.missions fieldset{display:grid;gap:.5rem;border:1px solid #ffffff24;border-radius:13px;padding:1rem;background:#ffffff0b}.missions legend{display:grid;gap:.2rem;font-weight:700}.missions legend span{display:grid;place-items:center;width:1.7rem;height:1.7rem;border-radius:99px;background:#6d64d8}.missions label{padding:.5rem;border-radius:8px;background:#ffffff0c}.missions button,.control-room button{justify-self:start;border:0;border-radius:8px;padding:.6rem .8rem;background:#f4c95d;color:#17152e;font-weight:900}.missions fieldset.restored{border-color:#76e0b7;background:#123d35}.missions p{padding:.55rem;border-radius:8px;background:#00000024}.control-room{margin:0 1rem 1rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #f4c95d;border-radius:13px;background:#28244a}.control-room label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font-weight:800}.control-room textarea{font:inherit;padding:.7rem;border-radius:9px}.arcade button:focus-visible,.arcade input:focus-visible,.arcade textarea:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #76e0b7;outline-offset:2px}@media(max-width:700px){.missions{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.power span{transition:none}}
</style>
